B.a2p=new A.b4([B.f4,"Basic horizontal stabiliser provides a restoring pitching moment. Simple and reliable \u2014 like most paper planes.",B.em,"Curved tail generates a small downforce at the rear, creating a nose-up moment \u2014 helping the plane maintain lift.",B.dN,"V-tail (split) maximises stabilising surface area. Real gliders use this for maximum efficiency and stability.",B.hp,"No tail = no stabilising moment! Very agile but unstable. For experienced pilots only \u2014 like a delta-wing fighter!",B.dO,"Swept-back tail \u2014 reduces tail drag while maintaining strong pitch stability. Best of both worlds.",B.d8,"Twin vertical fins. Used on high-performance jets (F-15, SR-71). Extreme yaw stability and superb glide ratio."],A.ab("b4<dS,B>"))
