B.a2N=new A.b4([B.ed,"Blunt nose creates a large stagnation zone (high pressure region). More drag but more stable \u2014 forgiving to fly.",B.dC,"Pointed nose reduces pressure drag by streamlining the leading edge. Trade-off: slight reduction in pitch stability.",B.dD,"Folded nose adds weight to the front, shifting the centre of gravity forward \u2014 a classic stability trick for paper planes.",B.dE,"Minimum drag, maximum penetration. But needs perfect balance \u2014 small errors in weight distribution cause instability!",B.cB,"Conical nose tip. Inspired by supersonic aircraft \u2014 pushes air aside with minimal drag. Requires perfect balance.",B.ee,"Rounded nose distributes pressure gently. Low drag at low speeds. Maximises stability on longer flights."],A.ab("b4<dP,B>"))
